Slurm opens --output/--error BEFORE the job script runs, so this directory has to exist in a
fresh checkout. `mkdir -p "$OUT_DIR"` inside slurm/p3/rnafm_stage2_finetune.sbatch is too late:
by then the job has already failed to open its own log files. Committing the directory is the
robust half of the fix — a submit-side `mkdir` works too but can be forgotten, and the failure
it produces (no logs at all) is the hardest kind to diagnose. Found by CodeRabbit on PR #134.
